        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): keep reconnect errors visible",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where iOS users reconnecting to a gateway would see the previous connection error replaced by “Reconnecting…” before they could read or inspect it.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nKeep the retained gateway problem ahead of reconnect progress in both shared status presentation and onboarding. Successful connections still win immediately, and reconnect progress still appears when there is no prior error.\n\nThis is AI-assisted work. The change and its state precedence were reviewed manually and with the repository autoreview gate.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe most recent gateway error stays visible while iOS reconnects in the background, giving users time to read the message or open its details. No reconnect behavior or retry timing changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused iOS simulator test: 9 tests across `GatewayStatusBuilderTests` and `OnboardingConnectPhaseTests` passed.\n- Testbox `quick-shrimp-d856` (`tbx_01kxcm2g1kx62tj5recerwkbcm`): `pnpm check:changed` passed against the rebased head.\n- Fresh branch autoreview against `origin/main`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `swiftformat --lint` passed for all five touched Swift files.\n- Real-device behavior proof unavailable: no physical iPhone was attached. Exact-head macOS `ios-build` CI is required before merge.\n",
